& [Purpose] replace residual string folklore with one exact inspectable compiled catalogue
  + schema residual references resolve to stable records
  + every record names where and how the non-schema condition is enforced or observed
  + schema acceptance never discharges a residual

& [RecordIdentity] is stable family plus number
  + RMS-R01 through RMS-R06 retain their exact established identifiers
  + I03-R007 through I03-R020 are the exact minimum successor families
  + identifiers are never reused renamed or silently merged
  + a split creates child residuals and retains the parent as a grouping or supersession record

& [RecordFields] are closed
  + residual id title class covered roots subject types applicability condition stage code bindings enforcement disposition I03 evaluation policy severity proof references related residuals and rationale
  + each code binding names crate module function set whole-source bytes and SHA256
  + file path and current line number are human locators only; module function and source digest are authority

& [RootIdentity] reuses MachineSchemaRootKind
  + prepare_input run_input verify_input base_response preparation_response
  + covered root means the root can carry the subject type or condition
  + applicability condition narrows when the residual actually governs an intended-use case

& [EnforcementDisposition] is closed
  + enforced means exact present code rejects or proves the full named condition
  + partially_enforced means a named portion is present and a named portion remains open
  + unimplemented means no acceptable enforcement exists
  + observational means the record describes non-capability or a limitation rather than a reader acceptance gate
  + outside_i03 means enforcement exists but I03 may not execute that authority stage

& [I03EvaluationPolicy] is safe_pure observational_only or prohibited_authority
  + policy never upgrades enforcement disposition

